From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dodaskot <pessdres@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 22:58:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 073/131] arm64: dts: a22x: microphones are DC-coupled

The stock DT sets no mic-type, so the vendor MT6359 driver runs the
microphones in its default DCC mode. With ACC the codec ADC returns only
zeros (the MTKAIF link, codec UL path and AFE were verified with their
test sine generators).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts
index b3da113b9..67cd9e03e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts
@@ -684,9 +684,14 @@ mt6359_accdet: accdet {
 
 			mt6359codec {
 				mediatek,dmic-mode = <0>;	/* two-wire */
-				mediatek,mic-type-0 = <1>;	/* ACC */
-				mediatek,mic-type-1 = <1>;
-				mediatek,mic-type-2 = <1>;
+				/*
+				 * DCC: the stock DT has no mic-type, so the vendor
+				 * driver uses its default DCC; with ACC the ADC
+				 * delivers only zeros.
+				 */
+				mediatek,mic-type-0 = <3>;
+				mediatek,mic-type-1 = <3>;
+				mediatek,mic-type-2 = <3>;
 			};
 
 			/*
